A||||4||DavidHenshaw||Mysterous 2.8 symptoms||||3||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||11-01-2000||10:20 PM||||After putting 3,000 trouble free miles on my 2.8 v6 something strange happened.<P>Had been driving awhile so engine was warm, pulled out into fast moving traffic and accelerated fast, hit about 50 mph and the engine died suddenly. Coasted to stop and tried to start. Engine turns over normally but wouldn't start. Check distributor and plug wires, all ok, won't start.<P>One hour goes by, verify gas tank full, still won't start. Three hours later, tow Fiero home, try to start, nothing, just turns over normally on starter. <P>Two days later it fires up like nothing was ever wrong. What gives?<P>Dave<P>86 GT<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||Seanh||11-01-2000||10:49 PM||||Sounds like maybe a bad ignition modual. Did you notice any odd tach readings before the car died? My car did that when the distributor bid the dust, but it wouldnt ever start up again until I replaced it. Did you check for any codes present? Do that and see what you find, even if the check engine light didnt come on, it might have stored a code.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||11-01-2000||11:31 PM||||Sounded like a module to me too.  I had the experience of my car just dying instantly.<P>Field check was to remove a plug wire and look for spark (none).  We could smell gas.  <P>That's the old shade tree mechanic test.  Look for spark and fuel.  <P>Modules can be tested at your parts house, but buy GM OEM if you need to replace.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||11-02-2000||10:17 AM||||Module and coil replacement fixed mine. (Probably only the module, but I chose to replace them both. Being stalled in Atlanta traffic <I>sucks</I>.)<BR>My tach jumped around before my engine died, and I *was* able to restart it, though. <BR>I've also heard of tach filters shorting, and killing the engine, but after I replaced the other stuff, I haven't had any problems.<P>Raydar<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||ROB MAC||11-02-2000||01:25 PM||||Happened to me in a Barracuda. Turned out the coil wire would cut out, then a day later it was fine. Faulty coil wire. My experience is when a coil or module go , they're toast...they don't start working later.||||reg||1
